4.—(1) The exemption under paragraph 3 shall be subject to the following conditions:
(a)every exempt film shall be used by the exempt institution or any exempt person for educational and research purposes only;
(b)the exempt institution shall keep and maintain a register of exempt films containing the title of every exempt film and such other information as may be specified by the Authority;
[S 347/2019 wef 29/04/2019]
(c)an exempt film shall be used only in such rooms within the premises of the exempt institution as may be approved by the Authority (referred to in this Notification as the approved rooms), and access to the approved rooms shall be restricted to the exempt persons only;
[S 347/2019 wef 29/04/2019]
(d)when any exempt film is not exhibited, the exempt film shall be kept or stored in a facility within the premises of the exempt institution which is safe and secure and to which only the exempt persons have access;
(e)neither the exempt institution nor any exempt person shall reproduce, distribute, promote or advertise on any media or platform any exempt film, or cause any exempt film to be so reproduced, distributed, promoted or advertised;
(f)Mr Adams Wai-Kin Kong remains in the employment of the exempt institution and deployed at the School of Computer Engineering; and
(g)the exempt institution shall allow any enforcement officer to enter the premises of the exempt institution at any time to inspect the register referred to in sub-paragraph (b) and to ascertain whether all the conditions of the exemption are complied with.
[S 347/2019 wef 29/04/2019]
(2) If any condition in sub-paragraph (1) is not complied with by the exempt institution or by any exempt person in respect of any exempt film, the exemption in paragraph 3 shall not apply to, or in relation to, the exempt institution and all exempt persons in respect of all exempt films.
